 "structural_change": "CODEX IDX6 structural lattice/channel and clock-mass redesign: prior s3r a/b failed TT/FF spread99.7/94.9 and94.9/88.3 plus GRT_RC2; original stack had y127.488/168.576 off43.2 lattice and0.024um channels. New literal R0 SRAM origins x86.4/y172.8,259.2,345.6, 45.336um vertical channels. All mapped soft cells fenced in one lower full-width149.04um band; 27600um2 measured source std area /50863um2 band=54.26% before CTS. All wide buses on lower W/E faces at <=5.49 signals/um, clock centered S beside compact register mass. 345.6x432 outline=149299um2, +166.67% over259.2x216=55987um2; four quadrant parent must grow. Same native32 source/ports/edges/calendar, +0 cycles. Actual placed band, reset, native census, reach, clocks and GRT required; sizing alone establishes no physical PASS.",
